WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:09.080
Impeachment we're told is similar to a coup d'etat. It's a dangerous distraction from the business of government,

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:17.500
that it's going to cause national trauma, a constitutional crisis, and even a second American Civil War.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.900
There's no reason to believe any of this.

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:26.800
Nobody likes to get fired right, but if there's any country on earth

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:32.760
that's pretty comfortable with the idea that people can be fired it's the United States of America.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:40.440
Not only are we basically okay with this, America actually pioneered the idea of firing people

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:47.580
as entertainment. You're fired. Now people often say that you know the presidency is such an important job,

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:54.100
it's such a powerful office that we depend on, it's so much that the bar to removing a president

00:00:54.100 --> 00:01:01.840
should be very high. It seems to me you know the logic works in the opposite direction. Somehow we've decided

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:08.780
that the one job in America that gets the most job protection is the one where you actually get

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:16.160
nuclear weapons, which doesn't seem at all sensible. It's time for this madness to stop, to put this behind us,

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:20.840
so the Congress can get on with the real issues. We should be tackling, real problems.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:25.160
We could have lower prescription drug prices today but Pelosi won't bring those bills to the floor

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:31.460
because she's infatuated with impeachment. And we are voting today perhaps to paralyze our government.

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:38.000
Yeah we always hear that impeachment might paralyze the federal government which,

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:44.180
you know for some of us isn't the most terrifying prospect. The fact is the business of government,

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:52.680
for good and for ill, goes along more or less as it has been during an impeachment process.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:02:01.360
In fact just before Thanksgiving the Congress voted to reauthorize the Patriot Act and extend NSA surveillance

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:08.540
and metadata collection. So for better or for worse impeachment does not paralyze the federal government.

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:14.800
This is a modern-day coup d'etat, Mr. Speaker. It's not easy to make a coup attempt boring,

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:19.880
but the Democrats found a way. It's a sham, a witch-hunt, and it's tantamount to a coup.

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:24.060
They have wanted to reverse the course of the 2016 election.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:27.040
The impeachment would only reverse an election

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:35.300
if it installed Hillary Clinton, in this case, instead of Mike Pence. And what kind of coup is it

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:41.820
that replaces an elected president with is also duly elected hand-picked running mate?

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:48.400
I hope that we will finally move past this nightmare. It's the political equivalent of capital punishment.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:52.940
I'm afraid it will cause a civil war-like fracture.

00:02:52.940 --> 00:03:00.100
These chambers will become the incinerator of the Constitution. Our long national nightmare.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:06.820
A lot of people really do think this is a national nightmare or some kind of regicide. Something,

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:10.020
something that we should only do in fear and trembling.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:13.960
The framers weren't nearly this emo about impeachment.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:21.240
Impeachment is a legitimate, peaceful, constitutional process by which the people's representatives

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:27.920
decide to give the president an early retirement before his term is up. Our limited experience

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:33.740
with presidential impeachment shows that they tend to demystify the presidency.

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:41.560
You are reminded that these are extremely flawed human beings and we've suffered no discernible harm

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:49.400
from our three prior serious attempts at presidential impeachment. And at least one of them

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:55.360
did quite a lot of good. I shall resign the presidency effective at noon tomorrow. Post-watergate Congress's

00:03:55.360 --> 00:04:02.020
didn't stop at driving Richard Nixon from office. They addressed a lot of the abuses that

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:06.140
he and his predecessors had committed while he was in office.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:13.340
You had a strengthening the of the Freedom of Information Act. You had the Foreign Intelligence

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:19.660
Surveillance Act to restrict government spying. You had the War Powers Resolution,

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:23.860
the National Emergencies Act, the Impoundment Control Act,

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:30.980
all of these flawed but sincere efforts to put the presidency back in its box,

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:36.460
and make impeachment serve as what it was supposed to be, as the Federalist Papers tell us,

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:41.740
a bridle in the hands of the legislative body on the executive servants of the government.

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:47.280
And the framers of the Constitution are rolling over in their graves crying out from heaven.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:51.320
Some of the same people who talk about, you know, the wisdom of the framers,

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:53.860
talk about the impeachment power

00:04:53.860 --> 00:05:01.200
as if the framers just decided to hard wire in a doomsday device into the Constitution.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:08.200
The framers didn't look at it that way, they saw impeachment is a necessary constitutional safety valve,

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:15.660
or something like an emergency brake on a train. It's not something you want to use on a weekly basis,

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:23.200
but it's nice to have it around when you need it. Ben Franklin at the Constitutional Convention

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:29.060
thought that including an impeachment power was actually favorable to the president.

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:33.900
It provided for regular punishment of the executive when his misconduct deserved it,

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:38.440
and for his honorable acquittal when he was unjustly accused.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:42.140
I think that's the way in which we should look at it today.

